{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_23e5e36be1bea4a5d315788e05af8ba3eb6e80a3dea2483e106ebe7081911aca"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Fusil is configured entirely through command-line options, grouped into categories like Input, Running, Fuzzing, OOM Fuzzing, and Logging; a former fusil.conf file mechanism was removed, making CLI options the single source of truth."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4592bb549b23f83420a8400a6ca4ce32f0fd9ec8acde3da26ae2be218a1d6006"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A few settings lack CLI flags — session scoring thresholds, the memory limit, and the dedicated fusil-user sandbox user/group — and live as constants in fusil/config.py's FusilConfig class."}],"claim_ids":["clm_23e5e36be1bea4a5d315788e05af8ba3eb6e80a3dea2483e106ebe7081911aca","clm_4592bb549b23f83420a8400a6ca4ce32f0fd9ec8acde3da26ae2be218a1d6006"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:46:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_d4e78f6adae347c781ce846edec4cc6b","id":"pg_0b63b126d76855249dc574ed9cd4b856","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/devdanzin-fusil-doc-configuration-rst-a7aa4e94bd84-74ed9cd4b856.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_eb9be3928d8e58ea85b5a009d3e6f303"],"title":"devdanzin/fusil/doc/configuration.rst @ a7aa4e94bd84","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:46:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d4e78f6adae347c781ce846edec4cc6b"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_191a5614ab2402f5d699d7900088eae5657cf07b3f65a867ee3998e4e045380a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: tests use unittest (python -m unittest discover -s tests), with ruff check for linting and ruff format for formatting."},{"claim_ids":["clm_36885c75776835396edd255e54c040c5cbc5b884977ec8d14c17afb9f3ac853f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"By default the fuzzer expects a dedicated unprivileged fusil user/group to drop privileges to; the --unsafe flag instead runs fuzzed children as the current user."},{"claim_ids":["clm_60b3ac5775ed024c98b40a56ae98239d58535e737f39c04012ecf9226edc2c6f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Fusil is a revival of Victor Stinner's fuzzing framework; only the Python fuzzing path is actively developed and tested, targeting crashes in CPython, C extensions, the Tier-2 JIT, and OOM error paths."},{"claim_ids":["clm_65ebc804fcc6cb3425d37d2aeb92ba373e5919dcbd8e1f139c5379484c53d1d7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Fusil requires Python 3.13+ and python-ptrace; numpy and h5py are optional extras supporting the argument generator, installed via pip install -e '.[numpy,h5py]'."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7889ad8225b9dc8a01328b15aa024f432e59bf3feb0a542921defac6ac53f608"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Each session generates a standalone test script, runs it as a sandboxed child process with memory/cpu/process limits, dropped privileges, and redirected output, watching for crash signals and patterns like 'Fatal Python error' or AddressSanitizer output."},{"claim_ids":["clm_aa563e86ab6aca14362c8cb5e3bc1076e43a953299049eae66c3154e5d4ac9b1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Historical non-Python fuzzers (firefox, php, mplayer) and subsystems like network, file/process mangling, and X11 are legacy and out of scope, kept under notworking/ directories and may not work as-is."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ded7ff974ce58369fa7759387d6c9730b6e88ff6e8e32a8cce2f061af2e66e66"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Fusil is built as a small multi-agent system where agents communicate via asynchronous messages, and a per-session score drives the fuzzer's adaptive aggressivity."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fa84d85ecf8d778e6a1a395d20d8cda77656f12ea60ef365279a38c1ab249212"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributions to any part are welcome, but active development and CI focus on the Python fuzzer."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fe0191540bf2cb3c1e9271d58be76337b8f04db15609c3f685ae25a439977253"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documented Python-fuzzer options include --only-c, --jit-fuzz, --oom-fuzz/--oom-seq, --deep-dive, and --no-memory-limit, with the full list in createFuzzerOptions in fusil/python/__init__.py."}],"claim_ids":["clm_191a5614ab2402f5d699d7900088eae5657cf07b3f65a867ee3998e4e045380a","clm_36885c75776835396edd255e54c040c5cbc5b884977ec8d14c17afb9f3ac853f","clm_60b3ac5775ed024c98b40a56ae98239d58535e737f39c04012ecf9226edc2c6f","clm_65ebc804fcc6cb3425d37d2aeb92ba373e5919dcbd8e1f139c5379484c53d1d7","clm_7889ad8225b9dc8a01328b15aa024f432e59bf3feb0a542921defac6ac53f608","clm_aa563e86ab6aca14362c8cb5e3bc1076e43a953299049eae66c3154e5d4ac9b1","clm_ded7ff974ce58369fa7759387d6c9730b6e88ff6e8e32a8cce2f061af2e66e66","clm_fa84d85ecf8d778e6a1a395d20d8cda77656f12ea60ef365279a38c1ab249212","clm_fe0191540bf2cb3c1e9271d58be76337b8f04db15609c3f685ae25a439977253"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:46:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_d4e78f6adae347c781ce846edec4cc6b","id":"pg_3b100d00307053a0873b6283b72541b6","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/devdanzin-fusil-readme-rst-a7aa4e94bd84-6283b72541b6.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_d36a932791495f3ca67aa940900a09c0"],"title":"devdanzin/fusil/README.rst @ a7aa4e94bd84","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:46:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d4e78f6adae347c781ce846edec4cc6b"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_80d223c57a2389a5c1e8eb4ee4960b0d1df8c97045dcf8c69fb4f890922b05ee"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Agents are objects that send and receive messages, are inactive by default until activate() is called, expose a live() method invoked each session step, and register event handlers via on_EVENT-style method names."}],"claim_ids":["clm_80d223c57a2389a5c1e8eb4ee4960b0d1df8c97045dcf8c69fb4f890922b05ee"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:46:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_d4e78f6adae347c781ce846edec4cc6b","id":"pg_a28a421970c354309facef69349911cd","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/devdanzin-fusil-doc-agent-rst-a7aa4e94bd84-ef69349911cd.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_48bdd13eb10a5ab6bb8176ba253bd69f"],"title":"devdanzin/fusil/doc/agent.rst @ a7aa4e94bd84","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:46:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d4e78f6adae347c781ce846edec4cc6b"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_b8013caa4297865fd780c1b22657b0b19dd6e42b0f4fbdb0cc2aee391cdeec05"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The architecture defines action agents (CreateProcess, StdoutFile, MangleFile, AutoMangle), network agents (TcpClient, UnixSocketClient, HttpServer), and probes such as FileWatch, CpuProbe, ProcessTimeWatch, WatchStdout, and Syslog."}],"claim_ids":["clm_b8013caa4297865fd780c1b22657b0b19dd6e42b0f4fbdb0cc2aee391cdeec05"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:46:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_d4e78f6adae347c781ce846edec4cc6b","id":"pg_ca69da5a5613583b8255a3ed9f00db6a","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/devdanzin-fusil-doc-architecture-rst-a7aa4e94bd84-a3ed9f00db6a.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_431446bdb1f3525b9aa246463cbf8fce"],"title":"devdanzin/fusil/doc/architecture.rst @ a7aa4e94bd84","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:46:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d4e78f6adae347c781ce846edec4cc6b"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_2f65d5ac2fd1e36d6113b6e549adcd9301c26808a6727e646ad7b866084866a3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The fusil.c_tools module provides C code generation utilities: CodeC with addMain()/addFunction() for building functions, a compile() method, and FuzzyFunctionC with value generators like createInt32, createString, and createRandomBytes."}],"claim_ids":["clm_2f65d5ac2fd1e36d6113b6e549adcd9301c26808a6727e646ad7b866084866a3"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:46:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_d4e78f6adae347c781ce846edec4cc6b","id":"pg_d69e7b127d6c5385960f9d0905239829","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/devdanzin-fusil-doc-c-tools-rst-a7aa4e94bd84-9d0905239829.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_3b4da4666499505685025435c2d2b7cd"],"title":"devdanzin/fusil/doc/c_tools.rst @ a7aa4e94bd84","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:46:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d4e78f6adae347c781ce846edec4cc6b"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_587c3096b2ca3b931c2af98fc7ee5650290eadd2b82b1fd0f197eb8ea7092126"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The memory cap was made ASan-safe: RLIMIT_AS is skipped when an ASan target is auto-detected or --no-memory-limit is set (since ASan reserves ~20 TB of virtual address space), relying on an external cgroup cap, while core-dump/nproc/nice limits are kept in all cases."},{"claim_ids":["clm_dec7f2c48fba5db8049b41a98bc03c6b1bafcf7f72c2fc80a199cf92358425b0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: a tech-debt plan records that CI (GitHub Actions running unittest and ruff check) was added after phases 0-7, with the suite green on Python 3.13 and 3.14 and grown to 308 tests."}],"claim_ids":["clm_587c3096b2ca3b931c2af98fc7ee5650290eadd2b82b1fd0f197eb8ea7092126","clm_dec7f2c48fba5db8049b41a98bc03c6b1bafcf7f72c2fc80a199cf92358425b0"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:46:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_d4e78f6adae347c781ce846edec4cc6b","id":"pg_e18ea3a087a954bfadfce5c89f990a3c","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/devdanzin-fusil-tech-debt-plan-md-a7aa4e94bd84-e5c89f990a3c.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_9c2b474ba6a454a294b9cb10c829ae5d"],"title":"devdanzin/fusil/TECH_DEBT_PLAN.md @ a7aa4e94bd84","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:46:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d4e78f6adae347c781ce846edec4cc6b"}
